{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1231262-black-spiral-dancer-question","id":1231262,"title":"Black Spiral Dancer question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-29T17:11:04-07:00","id":1231262,"title":"Black Spiral Dancer question","content":"I'm designing a BBEG. Can spirals be infected with bane spirits like fomori?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T01:52:45-07:00","id":1231317,"title":"","content":"As W20's Book of the Wyrm says, fomori are considered the lowest servants of the Wyrm. Some BSDs may consider letting a Bane infect them but to most a Fomor is nothing more but cannon fodder and thus they abhor the idea of being infected.<br /> Banes normally know better as to infect a BSD if they are not invited because they know how well armed Werewolfes are to deal with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T02:08:50-07:00","id":1231319,"title":"","content":"That said, high level BSD Gifts and rites can often do better than what fomori can do - it'd be perfectly within the bounds of canon for a Black Spiral BBEG to have a Gift to assume some powerful avatar form based on their Bane-Totem, if physical mutations to be more like a spirit-monster are what you're asking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T02:54:23-07:00","id":1231321,"title":"","content":"My very first game I ran ages ago with the coming of Revised involved a backstory of their Caern have a big war with a local Hive that ended with fighting a Nexus Crawler and the BSD's head Theurge binding some ancestor spirits and Banes into himself to die fighting as a seigemonster. Essentially in most situations where a BSD would be possessed by Banes I see it as a kamikaze tactic. They aren't becoming canon fodder so much as becoming a one wolf siege engine. Also their are unique situations were they can become reborn as Ferectoi, like being eaten and crapped out by Grandmaw Thunderwyrm, this originally I believe was supposed to be how Zhyzak got superstrength, I think they retconned it later to being the Green Dragon Blessing her.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also there used to be an Elder BSD gift that was Avatar of the Wyrm were you become essentially a boss fight. Zhyzak used to have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T09:17:58-07:00","id":1231382,"title":"","content":"Good suggestions here- Rite of the Flayed God from BotW20 is another way of gifting weird powers to Whippoorwill's bastards.<br /> <br /> Also, the possession could happen as a sort of 'stage 2' fight; once you villain lies dying, a powerful bane could take the opportunity to hijack the broken meat puppet and use the body for its own destructive ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T02:32:37-07:00","id":1231742,"title":"","content":"arent Enticer's and Toad's Given a bit of extra esteem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T23:18:06-07:00","id":1232053,"title":"","content":"I found the bsd gift to go saiyan mode. Didn't know about the retcon. <br /> I'll take this all as good advice. I'll consider this more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}